// C standard definitions (stddef.h)
// 
// This module is signature-only.
// 
// In Fun, most things from `stddef.h` are provided by C as typedefs/macros, so
// you typically *use the names directly* after importing this module.
// 
// Import:
// - `imp std.c.def;`
// 
// Common typedef names
// - `size_t`
// - Unsigned integer type used for sizes/lengths.
// - In Fun, this is treated as numeric-compatible.
// 
// - `ptrdiff_t`
// - Signed integer type used for pointer differences.
// - In Fun, this is treated as numeric-compatible.
// 
// - `wchar_t`
// - Wide character integer type.
// - In Fun, this is treated as numeric-compatible.
// 
// - `max_align_t`
// - An alignment type (usually a struct) available on C11+.
// - In Fun, this is treated as an opaque named type (not numeric).
// 
// Optional / platform-specific typedefs
// - `rsize_t`
// - Bounds-checked library size type (Annex K), if provided by the platform.
// - In Fun, this is treated as numeric-compatible.
// 
// Common macros
// - `NULL`
// - Null pointer constant.
// - In Fun, `NULL` is treated like the literal `0` for pointer assignment and
// comparisons (best-effort).
// 
// Notes
// - Function-like macros such as `offsetof(type, member)` cannot be expressed as
// Fun signatures today because they require passing a C type name, not a
// runtime value.
